 # Integration harness spawns publish Tattler endpoints into the real runtime directory
 
 devtools/integration/harness.ts isolates HOME, the agent dirs and git/jj config, but not the Tattler runtime directory: it neither sets XDG_RUNTIME_DIR nor TATTLER_RUNTIME_NAMESPACE, and inherits TMPDIR. Every entry:'sandpiper' spawn loads Tattler, which publishes a socket and identity file in the real runtime directory (on macOS, $TMPDIR/sandpiper). Live sessions can then list and message test sessions, and a test session can receive real peer messages. That breaks the repo rule that tests must not touch real user state. Found 2026-11-19 while probing TAT-68, which had to set XDG_RUNTIME_DIR and TATTLER_RUNTIME_NAMESPACE by hand. Fix: prepareIsolatedSpawn sets XDG_RUNTIME_DIR to a short per-spawn directory (Unix socket paths are capped near 104 bytes on macOS, so not under the long agentDir) and removes it on close; add an isolation assertion next to the config-isolation canary.
 
+## Outcome
+
+`prepareIsolatedSpawn` sets `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` to a fresh `/tmp/sp-rt-*` directory per spawn (overriding a caller's env, like the other isolation variables) and `cleanup` removes it; `IsolatedSpawn.runtimeDir` and `RpcSession.runtimeDir` expose it. Unit test in `harness.test.ts`; integration test in `config-isolation-canary.integration.test.ts` checks a real session's identity file and socket land there, and fails with the env line removed. README isolation list updated. bun check clean, 91 files/863 tests.
+
